  "worked_solution": "The sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series can be determined by the formula\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{{a}_{1}(1-{r}^{N})}{1-r}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, ${a}_{1}=-3$ and $r=\\frac{1}{4}.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{N} & =\\frac{-3[1-{(\\frac{1}{4})}^{N}]}{(1-\\frac{1}{4})} \\\\  & =\\frac{-3[1-{(\\frac{1}{4})}^{N}]}{(\\frac{3}{4})} \\\\  & =-4[1-{(\\frac{1}{4})}^{N}] \\\\  & =4[{(\\frac{1}{4})}^{N}-1] \\\\  & =4({4}^{-N}-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
